From 898335d154d85a63fd9bf4ad82bf4f73a260c61f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Billy Tsai <billy_tsai@aspeedtech.com>
Date: Wed, 2 Sep 2026 11:02:57 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] libocp: add INDIRECT_FIFO_CTRL/STATUS/DATA (v1.1 FIFO)
 support

Add the OCP Secure Firmware Recovery v1.1 FIFO indirect mechanism
(spec 8.2.5, commands 0x2D/0x2E/0x2F), previously rejected outright
with std::errc::not_supported:

 - indirectFifoCtrl(): selects a FIFO CMS window, optionally resetting
   its Write/Read indices, and declares the image size (rounded up to
   4-byte units on the wire).
 - indirectFifoStatus(): decodes empty/full, region type, Write/Read
   Index, FIFO size and max transfer size (all 4-byte units), plus
   spaceRemainingUnits() implementing the spec's exact
   "(ReadIdx - (WriteIdx+1) + FifoSize) % FifoSize" formula in native
   uint32_t so it stays correct if the free-running index counters
   wrap.
 - writeIndirectFifoData(): a single INDIRECT_FIFO_DATA write.
 - writeImageFifo(): chunks a full image through
   writeIndirectFifoData(), clamping to the device's advertised max
   transfer size and polling indirectFifoStatus() for enough free FIFO
   space before each chunk (flow control per spec's "monitor Write/
   Read Index" option, rather than an ack bit - the FIFO model has no
   ack bit).

Target::recover() and the CLI's PerformOCPRecovery now pick this path
automatically via ProtCap::fifoOnly() instead of refusing FIFO-only
devices.

Signed-off-by: Billy Tsai <billy_tsai@aspeedtech.com>

Upstream-Status: Pending
